            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "The data is the output of two studies. <br><br>\nIn study 1 we tested the hypotheses that: \n<ol>\n<li>Men are more likely to display the better-than-average effect than women, especially when comparing themselves to women. \n<li>Men who score high on the better-than-average effect also have a bigger tendency to explain things, especially when speaking with women. \n</ol>\nIn study 2 we tested the hypothesis that: \n<ol>\n<li>Women are more prone to the interpretation bias than men, especially when speaking with men.\n</ol>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
